# SD Core for Windows documentation
#
# THE MARKDOWN IS THE SOURCE. The .html and .pdf beside it are generated:
#
#   python  <sd4windows>\sdb_ai\sd64\gplbld\mkdoc.py --in . --out .
#   powershell -File <sd4windows>\sdb_ai\sd64\gplbld\mkpdf.ps1 -In .
#
# WHY THEY START IGNORED, given this repository deliberately has no
# no-binaries rule (owner, 26 Aug 2026).  Permission is not the same as
# advisability, and the two directions are not equally reversible:
#
#   - ignored now, tracked later  ->  delete two lines, commit.  Costs nothing.
#   - tracked now, ignored later  ->  the binaries stay in history for ever.
#
# So this is the direction that keeps the choice open, not a ruling on it.
# The cost of tracking them is real: each PDF is ~200 KB, so a one-word fix to
# a Markdown page would commit a quarter-megabyte of unreadable diff, and the
# repository would grow monotonically.
#
# THREE OPTIONS, and it is the owner's call - question 16 of
# QUESTIONS-2026-08-26.md:
#   a. leave this as it is and attach the PDFs to a GitHub release
#   b. delete the *.pdf line to track the deliverable, so a clone needs no
#      toolchain
#   c. delete both lines - the HTML is text and diffs readably, and a PDF is
#      one browser print away from it
*.html
*.pdf

# Windows shell litter
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
